From: SP11 Linux audio parity project
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: match GSL unsupported graph-cal policy

The recovered Qualcomm ACDB resolver and Windows GSL sources explain the
single rejected record in the SP11 graph-calibration aggregate.  ACDB emits
PARAM_ID_SPR_SESSION_TIME, a query-only parameter, in the 10,464-byte
non-persistent calibration body.  SPF consequently reports
AR_EUNSUPPORTED (3) for the aggregate after processing its records.

Qualcomm GSL deliberately treats AR_EUNSUPPORTED from non-persistent graph
calibration as a warning and continues opening the graph.  Linux currently
collapses every positive DSP status to -EINVAL, so the same reference
transaction closes the graph.

Preserve AR_EUNSUPPORTED as -EOPNOTSUPP at the common response boundary and
tolerate it only for the protected graph-calibration stage.  Other DSP
errors remain fatal and all other callers still treat the unsupported
result as an error.

---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@
 #include "q6apm.h"
 #include "audioreach.h"
 
+#define AUDIOREACH_DSP_EUNSUPPORTED	3
+
 /* SubGraph Config */
 struct apm_sub_graph_data {
 	struct apm_sub_graph_cfg sub_graph_cfg;
@@ -700,7 +702,10 @@ int audioreach_send_cmd_sync(struct device *dev, gpr_device_t *gdev,
 		rc = -ETIMEDOUT;
 	} else if (result->status > 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "DSP returned error[%x] %x\n", hdr->opcode, result->status);
-		rc = -EINVAL;
+		if (result->status == AUDIOREACH_DSP_EUNSUPPORTED)
+			rc = -EOPNOTSUPP;
+		else
+			rc = -EINVAL;
 	} else {
 		/* DSP successfully finished the command */
 		rc = 0;
@@ -1203,6 +1208,17 @@ int audioreach_send_protected_graph_calibration(struct audioreach_graph *graph)
 	cal = (const u8 *)graph_cal->data;
 	cal_size = le32_to_cpu(graph_cal->size);
 	ret = q6apm_send_oob_config(graph, cal, cal_size);
+	if (ret == -EOPNOTSUPP) {
+		/*
+		 * Match Qualcomm GSL's graph-calibration policy. ACDB can
+		 * include query-only parameters in this aggregate; SPF reports
+		 * AR_EUNSUPPORTED after applying the supported records and GSL
+		 * deliberately lets graph open continue.
+		 */
+		dev_warn(graph->apm->dev,
+			 "graph calibration returned AR_EUNSUPPORTED; continuing as Qualcomm GSL does\n");
+		ret = 0;
+	}
 	if (ret) {
 		ib = q6apm_send_inband_config(graph, enable, sizeof(enable));
 		ob = q6apm_send_oob_config(graph, enable, sizeof(enable));
-- 
2.43.0
